# Same-origin storefront media proxy (learned 2026-10-06)

**Invariant:** Customers who can open `selpic.com.au` but **cannot reach** `*.supabase.co` must still see CMS/catalog images.

## Evidence

Customer phone: `bmeyyierrvjbjikliheo.supabase.co` → Chrome “This site can't be reached”. Owner phone opens the same WebP fine. Site HTML loads; only Storage host fails.

## Fix (shipped)

- `/api/storefront-media?u=` — allowlisted public Storage fetch + cache headers
- `toSameOriginStorefrontMediaUrl` / `resolveStorefrontImageSrc` rewrite display URLs
- Wired on home hero/category, header logo, ProductCard, ProductGallery, SlidingBackground, Market S hub
- Catalog save unwraps proxy URLs via `canonicalStorefrontMediaUrl` (do not persist `/api/storefront-media?…` as source of truth)

## Do / Do not

**Do** — Keep CMS/catalog canonical URLs as `https://…supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/…`. Rewrite only at display/proxy.

**Do not** — Open-proxy arbitrary hosts; save proxied paths into Supabase CMS; blame Oct 5 admin/email deploys for this class of failure.
